    ✔ Bind tiles and alternative controls to the shared selected-recipe state.
        ✔ Display output icon/quantity, alternative indicator, and chooser/cycle control.
        ✔ Grey unavailable supported tiles without removing hover/focus/click interactions; add a non-color unavailable marker.
        ✔ Show unsupported state/reason and disable both placement actions without blocking inspection or alternative selection.
        ✔ Preserve explicit selection and release it through the agreed interaction.
    ✔ Implement search, keyboard focus, scrolling, and empty-result feedback.
        ✔ On hover or keyboard focus show output name, ingredients, availability, and interaction hints.
        ✔ List all one-execution deficits, accepted alternatives, and accurate tool/special-requirement reasons.
        ✔ Keep shift-click tooltips about the first execution, not a hypothetical maximum-batch deficit.
        ✔ Route ordinary and shift-click through the client native-operation coordinator and display concise refusal reasons.
        ✔ Use non-interactive missing-position outlines only if supported by existing UI; never materialize preview items.
    ✔ Update availability, deficits, and ordering after relevant inventory changes; world loading creates fresh recipe state.
        ✔ Resolve and validate native crafting-grid full-contents refresh coverage without packet interception; that path bypasses SlotModified/MarkedDirty and currently exposes only native rendering dirty-slot state. Do not claim complete event coverage until this is proven.
        ✔ Keep selection stable and defer visible reordering of hovered/interacting tiles until the interaction finishes.
        ✔ Revalidate clicks against current state even while visible ordering is deferred.
        ✔ Suppress overlapping local placement dispatch, refresh from current inventory via native notifications, and leave authoritative reconciliation to the game without custom request/result messages.
    ✔ Add focused tests for state/input behavior where automated coverage is feasible and record separate live-client cases for rendering/input that require it.
        ✔ Use existing localization conventions for new labels, unavailable/unsupported states, hints, empty results, and refusal messages.
        ✔ Replace any Phase 2 score fixtures in production wiring with real Phase 3 results.

Completion criteria:

